---
title: Railfence cipher
tags: tools
heading: "Rail fence cipher"
summary: >-
    Writes the message in a zigzag across a number of rails, then reads it off one rail at a time.
---
{% from "macros/tool.njk" import toolSection with context %}
{% from "macros/tool-frame.njk" import toolFrame %}
{% set filename = page.fileSlug %}
{% set intro %}
    <p>Also known as the zigzag cipher, it takes its name from the way it's written, like a fence built with horizontal rails. More rails make it harder to decode without knowing how many were used. Here it is with 3 rails:</p>
    <p data-pagefind-ignore="all">
        <code class="tool-example">WE ARE DISCOVERED. RUN AT ONCE.</code>
        <code class="tool-example tool-example--block">W . . . E . . . C . . . R . . . U . . . O . . .
. E . R . D . S . O . E . E . R . N . T . N . E
. . A . . . I . . . V . . . D . . . A . . . C .</code>
        <code class="tool-example">WECRUO ERDSOEERNTNE AIVDAC</code>
    </p>
    <p>More on the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rail_fence_cipher" class="text-convrtr">Rail fence cipher</a> Wikipedia page.</p>
{% endset %}
{% call toolSection(intro) %}
{% call toolFrame(filename, "Rail fence cipher", placeholder = "Example: HELLO WORLD &srarr; 2 [rails] &srarr; HLOOLELWRD", actions = [{ id: filename + "Encrypt", label: "Encrypt" }, { id: filename + "Decrypt", label: "Decrypt" }]) %}
<div class="tool-field tool-field--short">
    <label class="tool-field__label" for="{{ filename }}Amount"><span class="visually-hidden">Number of </span>Rails</label>
    <input type="number" class="form-control" id="{{ filename }}Amount" autocomplete="off" min="2" value="2" aria-describedby="{{ filename }}Status">
</div>
{% endcall %}
{% endcall %}
